  "term": "manic-depressive illness",
  "definition": "Manic-depressive illness, also called bipolar disorder, is a severe episodic condition involving disturbances in mood, thinking, and behaviour. The packet also links it to the brain systems that help regulate behaviour across different time scales and notes particular relevance to manic states.",
